    "children": [
      {
        "id": "demo-s1",
        "text": "Neurons & Layers",
        "type": "section",
        "layer": 1,
        "start": 0,
        "end": 300,
        "summary": "Networks are stacks of simple units that weigh evidence and pass it on.",
        "tone": [
          "instructional"
        ],
        "keywords": [],
        "notes": "Try it: click ▶ chips, press 1–4 to switch semantic layers, right-click for AI actions, or open 🎓 Study.",
        "links": [
          {
            "title": "Neural network (Wikipedia)",
            "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neural_network_(machine_learning)"
          }
        ],
        "image": null,
        "collapsed": false,
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "demo-s1-c1",
            "text": "Artificial neuron: weighted sum of inputs passed through an activation",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 42,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Each neuron multiplies inputs by weights, adds a bias and squashes the result.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s1-c1-d1",
                "text": "Weights scale how much each input matters",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 70,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s1-c1-d2",
                "text": "Bias shifts the activation threshold",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 95,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s1-c1-t1",
                "text": "“Think of a neuron as a tiny voting machine where every input gets a different number of votes.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 48,
                "end": 56,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "demo-s1-c2",
            "text": "Activation functions: add non-linearity (ReLU, sigmoid, tanh)",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 140,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Non-linear activations let networks model curved decision boundaries.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s1-c2-d1",
                "text": "Without them, stacked layers collapse into one linear map",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 175,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s1-c2-t1",
                "text": "“If you remove the activation, ten layers are mathematically no better than one.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 146,
                "end": 154,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "demo-s1-c3",
            "text": "Layers: input → hidden → output",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 220,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Depth lets networks build features from simple edges to abstract ideas.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s1-c3-d1",
                "text": "Early layers detect simple patterns, later layers combine them",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 255,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s1-c3-t1",
                "text": "“The first layer might see edges, the next sees shapes, and deeper layers see whole objects.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 226,
                "end": 234,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "color": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "demo-s2",
        "text": "Forward Pass & Loss",
        "type": "section",
        "layer": 1,
        "start": 300,
        "end": 480,
        "summary": "A prediction is produced, then scored by a loss function.",
        "tone": [
          "analytical"
        ],
        "keywords": [],
        "notes": "",
        "links": [],
        "image": null,
        "collapsed": false,
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "demo-s2-c1",
            "text": "Forward pass: data flows layer by layer to a prediction",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 320,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Inputs are transformed by each layer until the output layer produces a guess.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s2-c1-d1",
                "text": "Output layer size matches the number of classes",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 350,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s2-c1-t1",
                "text": "“The forward pass is just the network making its best guess with the weights it currently has.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 326,
                "end": 334,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "demo-s2-c2",
            "text": "Loss function: one number measuring how wrong the prediction is",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 365,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Training means making this number smaller on average.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s2-c2-d1",
                "text": "Cross-entropy for classification",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 400,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s2-c2-d2",
                "text": "Mean squared error for regression",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 425,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s2-c2-t1",
                "text": "“Everything in training exists to push this single number down.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 371,
                "end": 379,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "color": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "demo-s3",
        "text": "Gradient Descent",
        "type": "section",
        "layer": 1,
        "start": 480,
        "end": 720,
        "summary": "Weights move a small step downhill on the loss surface, over and over.",
        "tone": [
          "enthusiastic",
          "instructional"
        ],
        "keywords": [],
        "notes": "",
        "links": [],
        "image": null,
        "collapsed": false,
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "demo-s3-c1",
            "text": "Gradient: direction of steepest increase of the loss",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 510,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Stepping against the gradient reduces the loss fastest locally.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s3-c1-d1",
                "text": "Imagine walking downhill in fog, feeling the slope under your feet",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 545,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s3-c1-t1",
                "text": "“This is honestly one of the most beautiful ideas in all of machine learning!”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 516,
                "end": 524,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "demo-s3-c2",
            "text": "Learning rate: step size for each weight update",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 580,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "The single most important hyper-parameter to tune.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s3-c2-d1",
                "text": "Too large overshoots the minimum",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 605,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s3-c2-d2",
                "text": "Too small crawls and wastes compute",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 620,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s3-c2-t1",
                "text": "“Be careful: a learning rate that is too high can make the loss explode.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 586,
                "end": 594,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "demo-s3-c3",
            "text": "Mini-batches: estimate the gradient on small samples",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 660,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Noisy but cheap gradient estimates that also help generalization.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s3-c3-d1",
                "text": "One pass over the whole dataset is called an epoch",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 690,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s3-c3-t1",
                "text": "“Instead of looking at all million examples, we look at a batch of sixty-four.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 666,
                "end": 674,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "color": 2
      },
      {
        "id": "demo-s4",
        "text": "Backpropagation",
        "type": "section",
        "layer": 1,
        "start": 720,
        "end": 960,
        "summary": "The chain rule tells every weight how it contributed to the error.",
        "tone": [
          "analytical"
        ],
        "keywords": [],
        "notes": "",
        "links": [],
        "image": null,
        "collapsed": false,
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "demo-s4-c1",
            "text": "Backpropagation: chain rule applied from output back to input",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 745,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Gradients are computed layer by layer, reusing intermediate results.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s4-c1-d1",
                "text": "Automatic differentiation libraries do this for you",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 800,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s4-c1-t1",
                "text": "“Backprop is just the chain rule from calculus, applied very systematically.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 751,
                "end": 759,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "demo-s4-c2",
            "text": "Vanishing gradients: signals shrink through deep stacks",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 850,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Early layers barely learn when gradients get multiplied by small numbers.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s4-c2-d1",
                "text": "ReLU activations help gradients flow",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 890,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s4-c2-d2",
                "text": "Residual connections add shortcuts for the signal",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 905,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s4-c2-t1",
                "text": "“This problem stalled deep learning for years, which is a real limitation of naive deep networks.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 856,
                "end": 864,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "color": 3
      },
      {
        "id": "demo-s5",
        "text": "Overfitting & Regularization",
        "type": "section",
        "layer": 1,
        "start": 960,
        "end": 1200,
        "summary": "A model can memorize its training data instead of learning the pattern.",
        "tone": [
          "cautionary"
        ],
        "keywords": [],
        "notes": "",
        "links": [],
        "image": null,
        "collapsed": false,
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "demo-s5-c1",
            "text": "Overfitting: memorizing training data instead of generalizing",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 980,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Training loss keeps falling while validation loss rises.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s5-c1-d1",
                "text": "More data is the most reliable cure",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 1010,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s5-c1-t1",
                "text": "“Watch out: a perfect score on training data is a warning sign, not a victory.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 986,
                "end": 994,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "demo-s5-c2",
            "text": "Dropout: randomly silence neurons during training",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 1050,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Forces the network to spread knowledge across many units.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s5-c2-d1",
                "text": "Disabled at inference time",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 1080,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s5-c2-t1",
                "text": "“Dropout is like making a team practice with random members missing.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 1056,
                "end": 1064,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "demo-s5-c3",
            "text": "Validation set: an early warning for overfitting",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 1120,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Held-out data used to pick hyper-parameters and stop training early.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s5-c3-d1",
                "text": "Never tune on the test set",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 1150,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s5-c3-t1",
                "text": "“The validation curve tells you when to stop.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 1126,
                "end": 1134,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "color": 4
      },
      {
        "id": "demo-s6",
        "text": "Is Bigger Always Better?",
        "type": "section",
        "layer": 1,
        "start": 1200,
        "end": 1440,
        "summary": "Researchers still debate scale versus architecture and interpretability.",
        "tone": [
          "controversial"
        ],
        "keywords": [],
        "notes": "",
        "links": [],
        "image": null,
        "collapsed": false,
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "demo-s6-c1",
            "text": "Scaling debate: more data & parameters vs. smarter architectures",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 1230,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Bigger models keep improving, but at rising cost — critics argue for efficiency.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s6-c1-d1",
                "text": "Compute and energy costs grow quickly",
                "type": "detail",
                "layer": 3,
                "start": 1275,
                "end": null,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              },
              {
                "id": "demo-s6-c1-t1",
                "text": "“This is a genuinely controversial topic and people disagree strongly.”",
                "type": "transcript",
                "layer": 4,
                "start": 1236,
                "end": 1244,
                "summary": "",
                "tone": [],
                "keywords": [],
                "notes": "",
                "links": [],
                "image": null,
                "collapsed": false,
                "children": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "demo-s6-c2",
            "text": "Interpretability: why a network decides is still hard to explain",
            "type": "concept",
            "layer": 2,
            "start": 1330,
            "end": null,
            "summary": "Tools like saliency maps offer partial, sometimes misleading explanations.",
            "tone": [],
            "keywords": [],
            "notes": "",
            "links": [],
            "image": null,
            "collapsed": false,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "demo-s6-c2-d1",
                "text": "Important for medicine, finance and law",
